## Agents

| Agent | Role |
|---|---|
| architect | Design authority — plans, ADRs, system boundaries |
| code-reviewer | Plan-driven review against project conventions |
| librarian | Keeps `agents/` source-of-truth in sync with reality |
| engineer | Implements features and fixes |

> **Codex has no agent picker.** Invoke a role by asking Codex to delegate — e.g. *"use the architect sub-agent to plan X"* or *"have the code-reviewer review this diff"*. Roles load only when the project is **trusted** (accept Codex's trust prompt the first time you run `codex` here); untrusted projects skip the `.codex/` config layer and no custom role is available.

## Skills

- `grill-plan` — stress-test plans before execution
- `orchestrate` — drive an approved plan: loop engineer → code-reviewer per phase
- `{{PROJECT_NAME}}-ground-truth` — single source of truth for the project

> **Codex has no per-skill `/` entry.** Skills aren't individual slash commands the way they are in Claude Code. Run `/skills` to list what's available, or just invoke one by name ("use the grill-plan skill on …") — Codex also pulls a skill in on its own when the task matches its description. Like agent roles, skills load only when the project is **trusted**.

## Conventions

- No AI attribution in commits or PR bodies.
- Plan before code: architect plan + user approval before non-trivial implementation.
- Source of truth for agents/skills is `agents/`. Edit there, then run `bash agents/scripts/sync_agents.sh`.
